    <h2 id="the-name">Why nil.ski?</h2>
    <p>
      My mum is Polish; her surname is Kotowska. I grew up with a Swedish surname instead, but had I carried
      hers, it would have been <strong>Kotowski</strong>. Polish surnames like this change their ending:
      <em>-ska</em> for women, <em>-ski</em> for men.
    </p>
    <p>So nil.ski is my name, given the Polish ending I never had: Nils + -ski = Nilski.</p>
    <p>This site used to live at <a href="https://misiu.co">misiu.co</a>.</p>
